step Fly to Freewind Post
  only Warrior,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Paladin,Mage,Warlock
  zone Orgrimmar
  fly "Freewind Post"
  zone Thousand Needles

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Freewind Post

step Prate Cloudseer
  only Shaman
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Prate Cloudseer hides in a small cave in the canyon wall north-east of the post, on the way east.
  turnin 1531                         -- Prate Cloudseer: your Air Totem
  note Prate also starts Elemental Aid (Razorfen Kraul), the 33-40 chain to The Tempest's Weapons: forever/class/shaman/call-of-air-horde.

step Dorn Plainstalker
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Dorn Plainstalker waits on the mesa just north-east of Freewind Post, across the rope bridges.
  accept 1150                         -- Dorn Plainstalker: Grenka Bloodscreech, in the harpy den west of the post

step Jandia
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Jandia, the trade supplies vendor, stands inside Freewind Post's inn.
  accept 98070                        -- Jandia: the Screeching harpies of Roguefeather Den
  accept 98069                        -- Jandia: her stolen supplies lie in the same harpy den

step The Screeching Canyon: kill these as you meet them
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip West of Freewind Post, below Darkcloud Pinnacle, the harpies of Roguefeather Den (28-30). The Screeching Harpies, Roguefeathers and Windcallers there are Jandia's; her Stolen Freewind Supplies lie on the ground along the foot of the cliff and in the cave up on top. Grenka Bloodscreech (31) walks among them: thin out the harpies around her before you pull her, for Dorn's claw.
  kill 4101 quest 98070.2
  kill 4104 quest 98070.3
  kill 4100 quest 98070.1
  collect 279383 x8 quest 98069 @27.0,51.9 map 1441 -- Stolen Freewind Supplies, on the ground around the den
  collect 5843 quest 1150             -- Grenka's Claw, from Grenka Bloodscreech

step Jandia
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Back east to Freewind Post.
  turnin 98070                        -- Jandia, inside the inn
  turnin 98069                        -- Jandia, inside the inn

step Dorn Plainstalker
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Back across to Dorn's mesa north-east of the post, then take the lift down to the canyon floor. Dorn's next test, Rok'Alim the Pounder, is an elite: leave it.
  turnin 1150                         -- Dorn Plainstalker

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Shimmering Flats

step Stormheart
  when group 97985
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip These are elite mobs: grouping up is encouraged, look for people to do it with. Stormheart is a level 30 elite: most classes solo it at level 32, but you may need help. Skip it if you are alone: the route has you grind the XP back.
  tip Stormheart walks the canyon road east of Freewind Post's lift, on the way to the salt flats: kill him for his heart.
  collect 279186 quest 97985          -- Stormheart's Still-beating Heart, from Stormheart

step Moktar Krin
  when onquest 1146
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Take the lift down and follow the canyon east. Moktar Krin camps on the north-western edge of the salt flats.
  turnin 1146                         -- Moktar Krin
  accept 1147

step Mirage Raceway
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip The goblins and gnomes of the Mirage Raceway are neutral and give quests to both factions.
  accept 1110                         -- Kravel Koalbeard
  accept 5762                         -- Kravel's crate for Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn, later on the route
  accept 1104                         -- Fizzle Brassbolts
  accept 1105                         -- Wizzle Brassbolts
  accept 1176                         -- Pozzik
  accept 1175                         -- Trackmaster Zherin

step Shimmering Flats: kill these as you meet them
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip North-east of the raceway onto the flats. The Saltstone Basilisks (30-31) sun themselves north-west of it, and the Sparkleshell Tortoises (30-31) wander among them on the western flats; the Salt Flats Scavengers and Vultures circle the eastern flats. Every vulture drops a bone, about one tortoise in three a shell.
  tip Careful: Scavengers and Vultures use Execute when your health is low. The Sparkleshell Snappers (34-35) crowd round a half-buried ship in the north-east and are over you here: the Tortoises of the western flats drop the shells just as often, so stay with them. Take the venom from the Reavers (31-32) of the north half and leave the Scorpid Terrors (33-34) further south.
  kill 4147 quest 1175.1 @75.7,57.3 map 1441
  collect 5795 quest 1105 @74.7,56.4 map 1441 -- Hardened Tortoise Shell, from the Sparkleshell Tortoises of the western flats
  collect 5848 quest 1176 @87.9,65.4 map 1441 -- Hollow Vulture Bone
  collect 5798 quest 1110             -- Rocket Car Rubble, all over the northern flats
  collect 5794 quest 1104             -- Salt Flat Venom, from the Scorpid Reavers of the north half

step Mirage Raceway
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip South-west back to the raceway.
  turnin 1110                         -- Kravel Koalbeard
  accept 1111                         -- Kravel Koalbeard: his parts order goes to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet, later on the route
  turnin 1104                         -- Fizzle Brassbolts
  turnin 1105                         -- Wizzle Brassbolts
  accept 1106                         -- Fizzle Brassbolts: his letter goes to Martek in the Badlands, at 39
  turnin 1176                         -- Pozzik
  accept 1178                         -- Pozzik: for Gazlowe in Ratchet, later on the route

step Level 32
  when level<32
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip The flats' south and the silithid dig are 32-35, Desolace's quests 32-38. Still below 32 after the raceway's hand-ins? Back north on the flats, the Scorpid Reavers (31-32) roam among the basilisks and tortoises: kill them until level 32; leave the Sparkleshell Snappers (34-35) and the Scorpid Terrors (33-34) alone. Or, with a group, run the Razorfen Kraul dungeon instead.
  goto 75.0,60.0 map 1441 "Scorpid Reavers"
  level 32 grind 4140                 -- grind on Scorpid Reaver

step The southern flats
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip South of the raceway, the Saltstone Crystalhides (32-33) and Gazers (34-35) roam the far end of the flats.
  tip Careful: the level 35 Gazers can still be two over you: pull them one at a time from the camp's edge, never two together.
  kill 4151 quest 1175.2 @78.4,87.9 map 1441
  kill 4150 quest 1175.3 @77.1,88.4 map 1441

step The Rustmaul Dig Site
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip West of them the silithid swarm the dig site. Searchers and Hive Drones walk among the mounds; the Invaders (34-35) stay inside the hive cave. The first silithid you kill drops a Cracked Silithid Carapace: open it.
  tip Careful: Hive Drones call for help when they fall to 20% health, and the Silithid Ravager (37, rare) walks the dig: take the Searchers and Drones (32-34) outside first, then pull the Invaders (34-35) one at a time from the cave mouth.
  kill 4130 quest 1147.1 @69.8,83.3 map 1441
  kill 4133 quest 1147.2 @68.0,85.7 map 1441
  kill 4131 quest 1147.3 @64.8,86.0 map 1441
  collect 5877 x1
  accept 1148 item 5877

step Parts of the Swarm
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Keep killing silithid at the dig site for the heart, the talons and the carapaces.
  collect 5855 quest 1148.1
  collect 5854 quest 1148.2
  collect 5853 quest 1148.3

step Moktar Krin
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip North from the dig to Moktar Krin's camp on the western edge of the flats.
  turnin 1147

step Mirage Raceway
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip East to the raceway, on the way south to Gadgetzan.
  turnin 1175                         -- Trackmaster Zherin

step Gadgetzan
  zone Tanaris
  tip South from the raceway over the Tanaris border to Gadgetzan, the walled goblin town: learn its flight path and fly back to Freewind Post from there, which is quicker than the walk west across the flats, and the next guides fly straight to Gadgetzan.
  goto 51.6,26.0 map 1446 "Gadgetzan"
  getfp "Gadgetzan"

